  <section class="surface panel-pad math-ecai-bridge" id="mathECAIBridge" aria-labelledby="mathECAIBridgeTitle">
    <div class="panel-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">STEP 05 · ARCHITECTURAL CONTEXT · KNOW WHAT IS CONNECTED</div><h2 id="mathECAIBridgeTitle">Where this mathematics fits in ECAI</h2></div></div>
    <p class="math-stage-description">ECAI combines knowledge indexing, retrieval with source provenance, typed relations and review surfaces. This mathematical workbench demonstrates a separate, exact transformation-and-checking capability. A verified curve map is <strong>not automatically a verified relationship between documents, concepts or behaviors</strong>.</p>
    <div class="math-bridge-grid">
      <article><span class="math-bridge-status">Browser demonstration</span><h3>Shape reconstruction</h3><p><strong>Here:</strong> elliptic-curve samples → drawing transforms → Fourier contour. The renderer explains geometric composition; it stores no knowledge, defines no semantic relation and submits no server job.</p><button type="button" class="math-text-jump" data-math-jump="mathKernel">Return to the animation ↗</button></article>
      <article><span class="math-bridge-status">Native math workbench</span><h3>Exact relations between curves</h3><p><strong>Here:</strong> <code>ecai_math_curve</code>, <code>ecai_math_isogeny</code> and <code>ecai_math_pathfinder</code> represent curves, find bounded rational maps and check algebraic identities. Results are scoped to the job and its bounds.</p><button type="button" class="math-text-jump" data-math-jump="mathResults">Inspect mathematical evidence ↗</button></article>
      <article><span class="math-bridge-status">ECAI knowledge workflows</span><h3>Sources, retrieval &amp; typed relations</h3><p><strong>Elsewhere in ECAI:</strong> indexed documents retain source identities; retrieval provides supporting records; typed relation rules and reviews supply application meaning. These mechanisms are separate from Fourier drawing and curve-path proofs.</p><button type="button" class="math-text-jump" data-go="search">Open ECAI knowledge search ↗</button></article>
      <article><span class="math-bridge-status math-bridge-research">Research boundary</span><h3>From semantic claims to algebra</h3><p><strong>Not established by this demo:</strong> an explicit versioned mapping from semantic objects to curve data, relation-preservation rules, and a replayable binding back to source evidence or DamageBDD behaviors. Those need separate tests and proofs.</p><a href="https://damagebdd.com/ecai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ECAI architecture &amp; capability matrix ↗</a></article>
    </div>
